  "body": "Measured for e96a8d2d4 (threshold defaults kept): on 2000 segments of real Codex and Claude Code traffic, the false alarms left at the default thresholds are shapes, not values a threshold can separate from real names:\n\n- AstrLink Guard: Claude Code's `<total_tokens>N tokens left</total_tokens>` counter taken as a secret (9 of 10 extra hits at 0.5; one survives at 0.8), and long base64 blobs.\n- Privacy Filter: ISO timestamps inside file paths taken as ACCOUNT (7 hits at 0.5), a log line, a plugin id (`figma@openai-curated-remote`).\n\nRaising the threshold to drop these loses real names (see the commit body for the table). Each wants a check after the model, with a test that a real value of the same kind in the same place is still masked.",
