   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T20:17:20Z",
   "body": "I checked this against upstream b1e8eb15 using synthetic local-model findings, with matching sensitive-value controls. These are checks of the post-model filter, not a run of AstrLink Guard or Privacy Filter.\n\nThe supplied total_tokens form is retained when reported as SECRET or ACCOUNT. A full ISO timestamp inside a path, a substring cut from a longer base64 word, and the full figma@openai-curated-remote identifier are also retained in the tested label combinations. Numeric secrets, account numbers in paths/logs, personal names and email controls remain masked.\n\nThere are still unresolved boundaries: a whole base64 value can be indistinguishable from a real token, and a date-only span inside a path behaves differently from a full timestamp. The report does not include the exact log line or the models' start/end spans. The old unpublished fork candidate therefore is not a complete verified fix for this issue, and I have not published it as one.\n\nCould you provide one sanitized text per remaining false positive, its model/label and exact selected span (or start/end offsets), together with the threshold? That lets a narrow filter check preserve real values of the same kind. No real GGUF inference or threshold comparison was run in this follow-up. AI-assisted investigation.",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
